module std;

import core;

// Forge hosted standard-library root.
//
// `std` is layered on `core`. Hosted startup, console I/O, filesystem,
// networking, clocks, OS threads, entropy, and process allocator policy live
// behind platform/provider contracts rather than leaking target APIs into
// portable application code.
//
// Bootstrap hosted modules currently include:
//   std.console
//   std.args
//   std.fs
//   std.lock
//   std.time
//   std.string
//   std.collections.string_map
//
// The root does not implicitly re-export these modules. Applications import
// only the hosted services they use. File/lock/time/argument operations end in
// target platform providers; portable collection/string algorithms should move
// into Forge source as the compiler/runtime substrate becomes capable enough.
